  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It's given that <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>. It follows that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 230 Over 100 EndFraction b\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>230</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi></math>. It's also given that <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"60 percent sign\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math>. It follows that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction c\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi></math>. Since&nbsp;<math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 230 Over 100 EndFraction b\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>230</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction c\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi></math>, it follows that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 230 Over 100 EndFraction b equals StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction c\"><mfrac><mn>230</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 100 Over 60 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>60</mn></mfrac></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 23 Over 6 EndFraction b equals c\"><mfrac><mn>23</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math>. If <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, then&nbsp;<math alttext=\"c equals StartFraction p Over 100 EndFraction b\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi></math>. It follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction 23 Over 6 EndFraction equals StartFraction p Over 100 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>23</mn>\n<mn>6</mn>\n</mfrac>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>p</mi>\n<mn>100</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction 2,300 Over 6 EndFraction equals p\"><mfrac><mn>2,300</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></math>. It follows that the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> is approximately <math alttext=\"383.33\"><mn>383.33</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, of the given choices, <math alttext=\"383\"><mn>383</mn>\n</math> is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> if <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>, rather than if <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, and if <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math>, rather than if <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> if <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> greater than <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, rather than&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> if <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> greater than <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, rather than&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>.</p>",
